=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  menu-layout el -----------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Adopted 2026-11-14: no Figma frame. Rocky Linux: firewalld has$
# no rules to manage in hardn, so item 3 says so. The same on$
# AlmaLinux, RHEL, CentOS Stream and Oracle Linux.$
$
hardn  v0.4.0              https://github.com/abbott/hardn$
$
# Rocky Linux 9.6 (Blue Onyx) ##################################$
$
  [BOS-SAN-L01]            192.0.2.10$
                           182 days, 2 hours, 26 minutes$
$
  [*] Risk Level           Low ~ strong security$
$
  [+] User                 + non-root, sudo$
                             ~ passwordless sudo$
  [+] SSH                  + key-only, no root, port 2230$
  [+] Firewall             + firewalld running$
  [+] Kernel               + 6 items applied$
  [+] Auto Updates         + dnf-automatic, security$
  [-] AppArmor             uses SELinux$
$
----------------------------------------------------------------$
$
  Select an option         Mode Live$
$
   1) User                 Create, manage (sudo, SSH keys)$
   2) SSH                  Disable root and passwords, set port$
   3) Firewall             Manage firewalld, port listening$
   4) Kernel               Harden sysctl (network, kernel)$
   5) Auto Updates         Enable automatic updates$
   6) Run All              Queue hardening actions$
   7) Backup               Configure hardn backup$
   8) Configuration        hardn.yml, dns, ntp, syslog$
   9) System Details       View system info$
  10) Logs                 View hardn logs$
$
   0) Exit                 q to quit$
$
    > Option [0-10 or q]:$
$
$

